    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Josh Lowe** (71.68). **Gunnar Henderson** commands the top spot in our rankings, benefiting from a significant dynamic platoon advantage against Alcantara, while **Josh Lowe** serves as our premier \"speed-chaser.\" Despite batting ninth, **Josh Lowe** receives a major boost from the opposing starter's slow delivery, creating an elite stolen base environment that overrides his lower lineup position. We are also capitalizing on the high-run environment in the **Miguel Vargas** (66.77) and **Nolan Schanuel** (65.03) matchups; both benefit from a favorable wind and bottom-tier opposing pitching, with **Nolan Schanuel** effectively weaponizing the wind out to offset the moderate park factors. **Heliot Ramos** (65.34) remains a strong start for similar reasons, as his pairing of raw power and stolen base efficiency against a vulnerable Buehler makes him a staple in the outfield.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Marcell Ozuna** (61.17). While he cleared the 60-point threshold for a strong start, he was squeezed out by the sheer efficiency of our projected starters in stolen-base-heavy matchups. **Marcell Ozuna** ultimately hit the pine because his lack of baserunning upside couldn't overcome the favorable efficiency scores of **Heliot Ramos** or **Kyle Tucker** (58.53). We are monitoring the status of **Drake Baldwin** (48.73) and **Jacob Wilson** (56.02) closely; **Drake Baldwin** faces a daunting task against Kirby, and while **Jacob Wilson** benefits from favorable wind conditions, he is battling a tough strikeout profile from S\u00e1nchez. We advise managers to keep an eye on late-breaking weather reports, as the \"Wind Out\" factors boosting **Miguel Vargas**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Josh Lowe**, and **Heliot Ramos** could deflate if the direction shifts, potentially narrowing the spread between our starters and the high-floor options on the bench like **Andy Pages** or **Coby Mayo**.",
